# L §8.3 LOAD-PARSE: a file that isn't UTF-8 can't be parsed; `run` refuses it, the path as the run is given it. The
# twin of L8_3_reprint_not_utf8, which refuses it the same way (issue #13, T1's gap I-2). m.tally is written in
# Latin-1, so its é is no UTF-8.
=== options disk latin1=m.tally
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "café"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: file is not UTF-8 (m.tally)
